To fix the "Bucket not found" error and the missing column errors, you must perform two actions:

1.  **Update your Code:** I will update the application to use the correct database columns (`funding_amount_usd`, `open_to_collaboration`, etc.) instead of merging them into the description.
2.  **Update your Database (Crucial):** You **must** run the SQL script provided below in your Supabase Dashboard. This script will automatically create the missing buckets and columns for you.

### Step 1: Run this SQL in Supabase
Go to **Supabase Dashboard** -> **SQL Editor** -> **New Query**, paste this, and click **Run**.

```sql
-- 1. Create the Missing Buckets
INSERT INTO storage.buckets (id, name, public)
VALUES ('PROJECT-IMAGES', 'PROJECT-IMAGES', true)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET public = true;

INSERT INTO storage.buckets (id, name, public)
VALUES ('TECHNICAL-DOCS', 'TECHNICAL-DOCS', false)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET public = false;

-- 2. Add Storage Policies (Allows uploads/downloads)
-- Note: If policies exist, these might error, which is fine.
BEGIN;
  DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Public Images View" ON storage.objects;
  DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Auth Images Upload" ON storage.objects;
  DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Auth Docs View" ON storage.objects;
  DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Auth Docs Upload" ON storage.objects;

  CREATE POLICY "Public Images View" ON storage.objects FOR SELECT USING (bucket_id = 'PROJECT-IMAGES');
  CREATE POLICY "Auth Images Upload" ON storage.objects FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (bucket_id = 'PROJECT-IMAGES' AND auth.role() = 'authenticated');

  CREATE POLICY "Auth Docs View" ON storage.objects FOR SELECT USING (bucket_id = 'TECHNICAL-DOCS' AND auth.role() = 'authenticated');
  CREATE POLICY "Auth Docs Upload" ON storage.objects FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (bucket_id = 'TECHNICAL-DOCS' AND auth.role() = 'authenticated');
COMMIT;

-- 3. Add Missing Columns to Projects Table
ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS funding_amount_usd TEXT;
ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS open_to_collaboration BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;
ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS technical_details_url TEXT;
ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS achievements TEXT[];
ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS needs TEXT[];
```

### Step 2: Code Updates
I will now update your app to properly use these new columns and buckets.

