payload.text:
The error `42501: new row violates row-level security policy` means your Supabase database has **Row Level Security (RLS)** enabled (which is the default and secure setting), but you haven't created any **Policies** to explicitly allow users to write data.

To fix this, you must run the SQL script below in your Supabase Dashboard. I have also updated `Dashboards.tsx` to give you a helpful message if this happens again.

### **Step 1: Run this SQL in Supabase**
Go to **Supabase Dashboard** -> **SQL Editor** -> **New Query**, paste this, and click **Run**.

```sql
-- 1. Enable RLS (Ensure it is on)
ALTER TABLE projects ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE eois ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE news ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- 2. Drop existing policies to avoid conflicts
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Public Read Projects" ON projects;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Auth Insert Projects" ON projects;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Auth Update Projects" ON projects;

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Public Read Profiles" ON profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "User Update Own Profile" ON profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "User Insert Own Profile" ON profiles;

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Auth Read EOIs" ON eois;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Auth Insert EOIs" ON eois;

-- 3. Create New Policies

-- PROJECTS: Everyone can read, Authenticated users can create/edit
CREATE POLICY "Public Read Projects" ON projects FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "Auth Insert Projects" ON projects FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.role() = 'authenticated');
CREATE POLICY "Auth Update Projects" ON projects FOR UPDATE USING (auth.role() = 'authenticated');

-- PROFILES: Everyone can read, Users can only create/edit their own
CREATE POLICY "Public Read Profiles" ON profiles FOR SELECT USING (true);
CREATE POLICY "User Insert Own Profile" ON profiles FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = id);
CREATE POLICY "User Update Own Profile" ON profiles FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = id);

-- EOIS: Authenticated users can read and create
CREATE POLICY "Auth Read EOIs" ON eois FOR SELECT USING (auth.role() = 'authenticated');
CREATE POLICY "Auth Insert EOIs" ON eois FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.role() = 'authenticated');

-- NEWS: Public read
CREATE POLICY "Public Read News" ON news FOR SELECT USING (true);
```

### **Step 2: App Updates**
I've updated the dashboard to catch this specific error and guide you if the policies are missing.

