To fix the **Row-Level Security (RLS)** error and the **localhost redirection** issue (which is why you can't verify your email), please follow these two steps.

### Step 1: Fix Database & Auth Settings (In Supabase Dashboard)

1.  **Bypass Email Confirmation:** 
    *   Go to **Supabase Dashboard** -> **Auth** -> **Settings**.
    *   Find **"Confirm email"** and **Switch it OFF**. 
    *   *Why?* This allows you to log in immediately after signing up without waiting for an email or dealing with the broken "localhost" link.

2.  **Fix RLS Permissions:**
    *   Go to **SQL Editor** -> **New Query**.
    *   Paste and **Run** this script:

```sql
-- 1. Fix Profiles Table RLS
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can insert their own profile" ON public.profiles;
CREATE POLICY "Users can insert their own profile" ON public.profiles 
FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can view their own profile" ON public.profiles;
CREATE POLICY "Users can view their own profile" ON public.profiles 
FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = id OR auth.role() = 'authenticated');

-- 2. Ensure Projects are private to the creator (Researcher)
ALTER TABLE public.projects ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS owner_id UUID REFERENCES auth.users(id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Researchers can manage their own projects" ON public.projects;
CREATE POLICY "Researchers can manage their own projects" ON public.projects 
FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = owner_id);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Everyone can view public projects" ON public.projects;
CREATE POLICY "Everyone can view public projects" ON public.projects 
FOR SELECT USING (true);
```

### Step 2: Update Application Code
I have updated the code to ensure the **owner_id** is saved with every project, the dashboard correctly filters for **only your projects**, and your **name** is displayed prominently.

